  $900$ galleons.
]

How much did CS change? \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_

#block(width: 100%, stroke: (left: 2pt + rgb("#c00000")), inset: (left: 1em))[
  #set text(fill: rgb("#c00000"))

  Down by $700$ galleons.
]

PS: \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_

#block(width: 100%, stroke: (left: 2pt + rgb("#c00000")), inset: (left: 1em))[
  #set text(fill: rgb("#c00000"))

  $2100$ galleons.
]

How much did PS change? \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_

#block(width: 100%, stroke: (left: 2pt + rgb("#c00000")), inset: (left: 1em))[
  #set text(fill: rgb("#c00000"))

  Up by $500$ galleons.
]

DWL: \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_

#block(width: 100%, stroke: (left: 2pt + rgb("#c00000")), inset: (left: 1em))[
  #set text(fill: rgb("#c00000"))

  $200$ galleons.
]

#block(width: 100%, stroke: (left: 2pt + rgb("#c00000")), inset: (left: 1em))[
  #set text(fill: rgb("#c00000"))

  #grid(
    columns: (1fr, 1fr),
    gutter: 1em,
    [
      The floor of $70$ sits above $P^* = 60$, so it binds. At $70$: $Q_d = 60$ and $Q_s = 100$, an excess of $40$; again only $60$ bottles are exchanged, now at $70$. The sellers who make the sales are the lowest-cost ones, whose sixtieth bottle costs $P = 20 + \frac{1}{2} \cdot 60 = 50$.

      The same six regions from Q2 apply; only the price line moves from $50$ up to $70$. Buyers keep only $A$; sellers collect $B$ and $D$ on top of $F$.
    ],
    [
      #image("data:image/svg+xml;base64,", width: 100%)
    ],
  )

  #align(center, table(
    columns: 4,
    align: (left, center, center, center),
    table.header([], [*CS*], [*PS*], [*DWL*]),
    [Equilibrium], [$A + B + C = 1600$], [$D + E + F = 1600$], [$0$],
    [Floor at $70$], [$A = 900$], [$B + D + F = 2100$], [$C + E = 200$],
  ))

  $\Delta \text{CS} = 900 - 1600 = -700$ and $\Delta \text{PS} = 2100 - 1600 = +500$. Now $B$ ($600$) is transferred from buyers to sellers, and the same $C + E$ ($200$) is lost. The ceiling and the floor are mirror images: each moves $600$ from one side of the market to the other and destroys $200$, because each stops the same $20$ trades.
]

